      "normalized": {
        "apiVersion": "hololab.dev/v1",
        "category": "reconstruction/colmap4d",
        "description": "Assemble timed points, camera observations and image pixels into a strict complete colmap4d model.",
        "docs": "Three scalar application components, not grouped arrays. Layout: cams/{cameras,images,times,time_meta}; points/{points3D,points_t,time_meta}; pixels/images/<NAME>. Accepts bin/txt tables (bin preferred) and emits binary under model/sparse/0. Retains all IDs and exact int64 nanoseconds. No JPEG XMP time derivation.\n\nChecks complete time coverage, duplicate IDs, safe unique image names, pixel bijection and resolution, reciprocal observations/tracks, source-frame point time equality and track_centroid mean. Both metadata objects must declare the same spec/unit/convention/clock domain; recursively overlapping fields must agree. Unknown metadata is preserved. Single 8-bit RGB/RGBA SDR sRGB images are required; pixel decoding cannot prove historical color conversion. Finishes with colmap4d validate_full and strict warning handling. Entire model is loaded in RAM; provision memory for dense point clouds.\n\nComponents cannot masquerade as complete models. See README.md and the application profiles docs/colmap4d-components.md. Legacy grouped JPEG/XMP behavior remains frozen at 0.1.5 and is separately available as col4d/frames-to-colmap4d@0.1.0. No STG changes or training are performed.\n\nInput port identifiers are 4d_points, 4d_cams and 4d_images, matching the MegaSAM outputs. Types and on-disk format are unchanged.\n",
        "exec": {
          "shell": "set -euo pipefail\npython \"{{ pack_dir }}/merge_colmap4d.py\" \\\n  --points \"{{ inputs['4d_points'] }}\" \\\n  --images \"{{ inputs['4d_images'] }}\" \\\n  --cams \"{{ inputs['4d_cams'] }}\" \\\n  --output \"{{ outputs.model }}\"\n"
        },
        "idempotency": {
          "marker": "{{ outputs.model }}/.hololab-done"
        },
